| 67.92 | % of pedestrian–vehicle interactions in which driver yielded | New Delhi; n=452 interactions; data year NR | One midblock crossing; geometry NR | Khan et al., [publisher abstract](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s41062-026-02547-8) | “drivers yield in 67.92% of total interactions” | FACT; **UNVERIFIED** study details | **No**—abstract only |

Neither source supplies a verified car/bus/2W/auto yield breakdown. The two rates use different sites and study definitions; they must not be pooled. Chaudhari et al. report that yielding varies with approach speed and geometry, but give no checked yield-by-speed table.

